lass=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c73\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c69\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2061\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-texatom space=\"2\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c63\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c6F\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c73\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2061\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-texatom space=\"2\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"NONE\">⁡</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>cos</mi><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"NONE\">⁡</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>t</mi></mrow></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></div></div></div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyModerate\">M</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Thu, Oct 15th @ 6:22 PM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:14</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: green;\">Correct</span></span></div></div>"
    },
    {
      "dom_id": "question-345086",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(t)-y(t)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y(0)=3,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=2\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n{s}^{2}Y(s)-3s-2-Y(s)=-4(\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1})-6(\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}).\n$$\n\nThe solution is $y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)-3s-2-Y(s) & =-4(\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1})-6(\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}) \\\\ ({s}^{2}-1)Y(s) & =3s+2-\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+1}-\\frac{6s}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ ({s}^{2}-1)Y(s) & =\\frac{(3s+2)({s}^{2}-1)}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{3s+2}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{3s}{{s}^{2}+1}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is valid for $s>1.$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}(Y(s)) & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{3s}{{s}^{2}+1}+\\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+1}\\} \\\\  & =3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}\\}+2{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}\\} \\\\  \\\\ y(t) & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
