      "dom_id": "question-345082",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(t)+y(t)=4{t}^{3}+24t,\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n{s}^{2}Y(s)+Y(s)=\\frac{24(1+{s}^{2})}{{s}^{4}}.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)+Y(s) & =\\frac{24(1+{s}^{2})}{{s}^{4}} \\\\ ({s}^{2}+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{24(1+{s}^{2})}{{s}^{4}} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{24}{{s}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is valid for $s>0.$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}(Y(s)) & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{24}{{s}^{4}}\\} \\\\ y(t) & =4{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}\\} \\\\ y(t) & =4{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
